[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Scotch Game"]
[Variation "Horwitz Attack"]
[ECO "C45"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "early-queen"]
[Themes "development-lead"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Qh4 { Black's queen comes out early and attacks the e4 pawn. }
5. Nb5 { Threatens Nxc7+, which would fork king and rook. It also moves the knight away from the queen's attack. [%cal Gb5c7] }
5... Bb4+ 6. Bd2 { Blocks the check and offers a bishop trade, so Black's bishop cannot take the knight on c3 later. } 6... Qxe4+
7. Be2 { Blocks the check. White is a pawn down but has more pieces developed. } 7... Kd8 8. O-O { The king is safe and the rook joins the game. } 8... Bxd2
9. Qxd2 9... a6 { Attacks the knight on b5. }
10. N5c3 { Both retreats the knight and attacks the queen, so White gains a tempo (a free move). [%cal Gc3e4] } 10... Qe5
11. Rfe1 { Puts the rook on the open e-file with tempo, because the queen on e5 is now attacked. } 11... Qd4 *
